'-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Cal01: Automatic hand-eye calibration
'
' Cambrian's Example 02 with the three setup steps that are easy to miss.
'
' BEFORE RUNNING
'   1. Rig pose verified with Chk02 - the triad's GREEN axis lines up with
'      "up" on the real cameras. A 180 deg axial flip in the initial estimate
'      will NOT converge.
'   2. REMOVE THE GRIPPER. At the calibration pose it clips the edge of the
'      field of view and partially occludes the board. The images still look
'      fine, so this is easy to miss and it wrecks the result.
'   3. Calibration board placed tangential to the robot base, no obstacles,
'      fully visible in both cameras from the start pose.
'   4. Cameras exposed so the board is clearly visible - manual exposure is
'      often more stable than auto for calibration capture.
'   5. Cable slack for full J6 rotation. The sweep rotates the wrist hard.
'
' WHAT THE TWO EXTRA LINES DO
'   CamSetCalibrationMount "FLANGE"
'     Sets robot-mounted explicitly rather than trusting the Cameras panel.
'     If the mount type is wrong the calibration result is wrong.
'
'   CamNewCalibration
'     Discards the existing rig calibration. This matters more than it looks:
'     Cambrian locks the PREVIOUS calibration's principal point as a reference
'     on every recalibration. If your first run was done with a bad rig pose,
'     every run since has been anchored to that bad data.
'
' AFTER IT FINISHES - acceptance numbers
'
'   Number of images    minimum 8      good 15+
'   Position STD        maximum 10 mm  good < 1 mm
'   Average pixel error maximum 10 px  good < 5 px
'
'   Then open the overlap diagnostic and zoom in:
'     ~/Desktop/Caint/Calibration/calib_X/results/unity/final_overlap.png
'     red dots        excellent
'     short red lines acceptable
'     long red lines  bad - recalibrate
'
'   If the numbers fail, do not proceed. Everything downstream depends on this.
'-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

#Include "Cambrian_API.pcs"

Sub Main
    TakeArm Keep = 1

    Dim CalibrationPose As Joint

'   Rig centre relative to the flange (mm) - carry over the values confirmed
'   with Chk02_RigPoseIterate.pcs
    Dim Tx As Single = 0
    Dim Ty As Single = -50
    Dim Tz As Single = 70
    Dim Rx As Single = 0
    Dim Ry As Single = 0
    Dim Rz As Single = 180

'   Standard rig geometry - change for small, wide or custom rigs
    Dim FocalLength As Single = 8          ' mm
    Dim StereoSeparation As Single = 0.08  ' METRES
    Dim Tilt As Single = 5                 ' degrees

    MOTOR ON

'   Teach J1 on the pendant: jog until the cameras frame the board, then save
'   the current pose into J1.
    CalibrationPose = J1

'   @0 and no Next, so the move blocks and the robot is fully stopped before
'   the solve begins.
    MOVE P, @0 CalibrationPose, SPEED=(100,100,100)

    CamInit 8
    CamPing

    CamSetCalibrationMount "FLANGE"
    CamNewCalibration

    CamAutoCalibration Tx, Ty, Tz, Rx, Ry, Rz, FocalLength, StereoSeparation, Tilt
End Sub
